    schema:description "InfluxData is the creator of InfluxDB, the leading time series platform used to collect, store, and analyze all time series data at any scale. Developers can query and analyze their time-stamped data in real-time to discover, interpret, and share new insights to gain a competitive edge. InfluxData is a remote-first company with a globally distributed workforce. For more information, visit www.influxdata.com. Are you fascinated by the Internet of Things (IoT), real-time analytics, and the systems that keep factories, vehicles, energy grids and software infrastructure running? Are you a recent graduate who loves to code, learns fast, and wants to work at the intersection of engineering and customers? InfluxData is looking for an Associate Sales Engineer to join our EMEA team — someone with a love of technology and a passion for helping customers discover what's possible. This is an early-career role. We don't expect you to have done this job before. We will teach you the craft of sales engineering; you bring the technical curiosity, the coding ability, and the appetite. This is a remote position based in the UK. Unlike our senior Sales Engineers, this role does not require regular customer site visits. You will work with customers remotely and alongside senior Sales Engineers, often building solutions on a customer's behalf — with occasional travel for team meetings, conferences and meetups. What you'll be doing Develop deep, hands-on expertise in InfluxDB and the wider InfluxData platform — including our APIs, client libraries, and integrations with tools like Telegraf, Grafana, MQTT and industrial protocols Partner with senior Sales Engineers on active opportunities: building demos, proof-of-concept environments, sample integrations and scripts on behalf of prospects and customers Provide responsive technical coverage across the sales team — answering product questions, running standard demos, and unblocking opportunities so senior SEs can focus on complex deals Contribute to formal RFx responses and informal prospect Q&A/workshop sessions Be an advocate for prospects and customers with our Engineering, Product and Support teams — relaying what you hear on the front line Write content for blogs, community forums and sample-code repositories Learn the mechanics of enterprise software sales (discovery, qualification, MEDDIC) from an experienced team What we're looking for A degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, Physics or a related discipline — or equivalent demonstrable technical ability. Comfortable writing code in at least one of Python, Go, JavaScript/Node.js or Java — enough to build working examples, integrations and small tools. Show us something you've built: side projects, hackathon entries, open-source contributions or coursework you're proud of all count. If you have supporting material, please submit that as part of your application. Familiarity with Linux fundamentals and the command line Some exposure to working with data — SQL, NoSQL, CSVs and scripts, or data coursework Excellent communication skills: you can explain a technical concept simply, to a technical or non-technical audience, in writing and in person Curiosity about how businesses and physical operations work — one week you might be learning about battery telemetry, the next about network monitoring Comfort with ambiguity and a bias for figuring things out: the best people in this role treat \"I don't know yet\" as the start of the fun Fluent written and spoken English Bonus points if you have Tinkered with hardware, sensors or microcontrollers — Raspberry Pi, Arduino, home automation, robotics, vehicles Any exposure to IoT or industrial technologies: MQTT, OPC-UA, SCADA, PLCs, telemetry Used monitoring or observability tools such as Grafana, Prometheus or InfluxDB itself Experience with Docker, Kubernetes or a cloud provider (AWS, Azure, GCP) Built anything with LLMs or AI developer tools Spoken/written fluency in other European languages If you’ve recently graduated, an internship or placement year is viewed very favourably How you'll grow You will be paired with senior Sales Engineers who will mentor you on both the technical and commercial sides of the role. Expect a structured ramp: product training and certification first, then shadowing live deals, then owning your own technical engagements. The path from Associate SE leads to Sales Engineer and beyond — into senior pre-sales, solutions architecture, product or engineering, depending on where your strengths take you. Interview Information: Our interview process begins remotely. Interviews are typically conducted via Zoom. To ensure every candidate can participate, please let us know if you are unable to access Zoom. Some roles may require an in-person meeting with a team member as part of the final stage. Our Core Values Our employees are the heart of the company and only by having a core set of beliefs and values will we be successful. We hire and live by these core values: We value each other We get stuff done We believe humility drives learning We embrace failure We are committed to open source Visit our careers page to learn more about working at InfluxData. To view our CCPA policies click HERE If you are a qualified individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, you may request a reasonable accommodation if you are unable or limited in your ability to use or access this website to apply for a vacancy as a result of your disability. You can request reasonable accommodations by reaching out to the recruiting team by emailing InfluxData does not accept unsolicited resumes from headhunters and recruitment agencies through our website, job board or directly to employees. InfluxData will not pay fees to any third-party agency, headhunter or company that does not have a signed agreement for this position in place. Beware of job scams and fraudulent offers! Our recruiters use @influxdata.com email addresses exclusively. We do not conduct interviews via text or instant message and we do not ask candidates to download software other than Zoom, to purchase equipment through us, or to provide sensitive personally identifiable information such as bank accounts or social security numbers. If you have been contacted by someone claiming to be from InfluxData from a different domain about a job offer, please report it as potential job fraud to law enforcement and to Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
