    schema:description "Company Description We’re Checkout.com. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started. We're looking for a proactive and operationally-minded Global People Operations Manager to help shape the future of People Operations at Checkout.com. This role sits at the centre of our global People function, connecting people strategy, regional requirements and technology to ensure our operations are scalable, compliant and deliver a seamless employee experience. You'll work across every part of the People organisation, partnering with Regional People Directors, People Partners, Process Architects & Knowledge Leads, and People Technology to transform complex operational challenges into simple, effective solutions. From driving AI adoption and operational automation, to leading global audits, business continuity planning and the evolution of our People Service Desk, you'll play a key role in modernising how we operate while ensuring strong governance, security and compliance. If you enjoy improving processes, influencing stakeholders and building operational excellence at scale, this is an opportunity to make a meaningful impact across a global organisation. Key Responsibilities Future of People Operations & Operational Excellence Champion an AI-first and automation-first approach to People Operations, embedding scalable, efficient ways of working that improve both the employee and People team experience. Drive adoption of Checkout.com's AI ecosystem, including Glean, Gemini, ChatGPT and Claude, helping colleagues build confidence and capability in using AI to improve productivity. Partner with our Knowledge managers on our People Operations knowledge strategy, ensuring processes, guidance and operational content are maintained and surfaced through Glean to enable a best-in-class self-service experience. Strategic Operations, Risk & Compliance Lead People Business Continuity Planning (BCP), ensuring robust plans are in place to support critical People operations during business disruption. Own the end-to-end audit process for the People function, partnering with internal and external auditors, coordinating evidence, tracking actions and ensuring timely remediation. Govern access management across People Technology platforms. Maintain a least-privilege approach through regular access reviews and approval processes. Represent relevant Checkout entities within quarterly Risk Committee meetings, preparing accurate reporting, risk assessments and supporting documentation for Board review. Partner with Regional People Directors to operationalise changes arising from employment law or regulatory updates, ensuring systems and processes remain aligned while compliance ownership remains within the regions. Process Design & Technology Own the ongoing development of the People Service Desk (JSM), using operational data and employee insights to improve service delivery, reduce friction and increase self-service. Partner with People Leadership and People Technology to maintain a balanced roadmap, ensuring initiatives are delivered while continually identifying opportunities to leverage automation and emerging technologies. Partner with People Technology to monitor roadmap delivery, communicate progress and ensure priorities remain aligned with business needs. Act as the operational bridge between Process Architects and regional People teams, consolidating global requirements while ensuring regional differences are appropriately reflected in solution design. Content & Policy Governance Lead the governance of People policies, ensuring they are clear, informative, well-structured, and reflective of both Checkout.com's values and the needs of our employees. Ensure all policies remain compliant with applicable global and local employment laws, regulatory requirements, and evolving legislative changes, while maintaining consistency across regions where appropriate. Partner with the Global Content Manager to maintain a consistent global policy framework, ensuring regional variations are accurately reflected where required. Support the governance of operational content through standardised templates, structured review cycles and ongoing policy maintenance. Program Leadership Lead key operational programmes throughout the year, including the annual policy review cycle, Annual Leave Cash Out & Carry Over and the employee on-call process. Work closely with People Partners and COEs to identify operational pain points, translating business needs into clear requirements and prioritised roadmap initiatives to improve global processes. About You You'll thrive in this role if you're someone who enjoys solving operational problems, bringing structure to complexity and working across multiple teams to deliver meaningful change. What you’ll bring to the role Experience in People Operations within a fast-paced, global or regulated environment. A passion for operational excellence, with a natural curiosity for improving processes through technology, automation and AI. Strong analytical skills, using operational data, audit findings and service metrics to identify trends and drive continuous improvement. Excellent stakeholder management skills, with the ability to build trusted relationships across technical, operational and business teams. A solid understanding of governance, risk management, data privacy and access control principles. Practical knowledge of employment legislation (particularly within the UK) and experience translating regulatory change into operational processes. A builder's mindset, you look beyond today's process to design scalable solutions that will continue to work as the business grows. Additional Information Bring all of you to work We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one. Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands. We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here. It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable. Life at Checkout.com We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection. Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our Careers Page to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us. For a closer look at daily life at Checkout.com, follow us on LinkedIn and Instagram Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
