    schema:description "Company Description We’re Checkout.com. You might not know our name, but companies like eBay, Spotify, Klarna, Uber, and Sony do, because we’re behind many of the digital experiences you use every day. We are where the world checks out, enabling over 10 billion transactions yearly for more than one billion global shoppers. Whether you want to book a holiday, order food, renew a subscription, or check out online, there’s a good chance our tech powers the payments behind the scenes. Our platform helps the most ambitious businesses deliver effortless digital experiences, at scale. If you want to do career-defining work, you’ve come to the right place. We move fast, think globally, and believe great teams are built by hiring exceptional people with conviction, curiosity, and the desire to make an impact. With 20 offices across six continents and London as our HQ, we’re shaping the future of fintech – and we’re just getting started. The Opportunity This is an excellent opportunity to be a key member of our core Finance team in London. As a Finance Transformation Senior Associate, you will play a pivotal role in strengthening our core accounting capabilities and shaping the future of our financial processes. You will be instrumental in delivering critical transformation projects, with a specific focus on building out our Transactional Ledger and achieving an accelerated financial close for Checkout. If you are a proactive and data-savvy finance professional with a passion for process improvement, this role is for you. Key Responsibilities Project Delivery & Support: Support and drive key workstreams within finance transformation projects, ensuring tasks are completed on time and to a high standard. You will be actively involved in the end-to-end project lifecycle, from analysis to implementation. Process Optimisation: Use data analysis to scrutinise existing \"as-is\" accounting processes, particularly those related to the financial close and transactional ledger, to quantitatively identify inefficiencies and control gaps. You will help design and implement standardised and scalable \"to-be\" processes. Change Management: Contribute to change management activities by preparing documentation, supporting user training sessions, and acting as a point of contact for queries to ensure smooth transitions and user adoption of new processes and systems. Stakeholder Engagement: Collaborate effectively with various stakeholders across local and global finance teams. Build strong working relationships to ensure project alignment and support successful outcomes. Governance & Control: Support the implementation and maintenance of a robust control framework for all new processes, ensuring compliance with internal policies and international accounting standards (e.g., IFRS). Performance Monitoring: Track and report on key performance indicators (KPIs) to help measure the success of transformation initiatives and ensure project benefits are realised. Required Skills & Experience Strong Accounting Knowledge: A professional accounting qualification (ACCA, ACA, CIMA, or equivalent) is mandatory. You must have a solid understanding of core accounting principles, month-end close procedures, and financial controls. Data Analytics & BI Skills: Proficiency in working with large, complex datasets is essential. Experience with data analytics tools is highly advantageous, particularly: SQL for data querying and manipulation. Python (especially libraries like Pandas) for data analysis. Business Intelligence packages such as Looker or Power BI for visualisation and reporting. Proven Transformation Experience: Demonstrable experience contributing to finance change or process improvement projects within a fast-paced environment. Experience with financial close optimisation, general ledger systems, or process standardisation is highly desirable. Strong Project & Organisational Skills: Proven ability to manage your own tasks and workstreams across multiple projects concurrently. You must be highly organised, detail-oriented, and adept at meeting deadlines. Industry Experience: Prior experience in the Fintech or Payments industry is advantageous. Excellent Stakeholder Management: Strong communication and interpersonal skills. You must be comfortable and credible when engaging with stakeholders at various levels of the organisation. Resilience & Adaptability: A proactive, \"can-do\" attitude with the ability to thrive under pressure and navigate ambiguity. You are a natural problem-solver who sees challenges as opportunities. Fluency in English is required. Additional Information Bring all of you to work We create the conditions for high performers to thrive, through real ownership, fewer blockers, and work that makes a difference from day one. Here, you’ll move fast, take on meaningful challenges, and be recognized for the impact you deliver. It’s a place where ambition gets met with opportunity, and where your growth is in your hands. We work as one team, and we back each other to succeed. So whatever your background or identity, if you’re ready to grow and make a difference, you’ll be right at home here. It’s important we set you up for success and make our process as accessible as possible. So let us know in your application, or tell your recruiter directly, if you need anything to make your experience or working environment more comfortable. Life at Checkout.com We understand that work is just one part of your life. Our hybrid working model offers flexibility, with three days per week in the office to support collaboration and connection. Curious about what it’s like to be part of our team? Visit our Careers Page to learn more about our culture, open roles, and what drives us. For a closer look at daily life at Checkout.com, follow us on LinkedIn and Instagram Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
