    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "senior-data-analyst-reporting-insights-hamburg-29540" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-22"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "At Statista, we’re all about facts and data, for we are the world's leading business data platform. By providing reliable and easy-to-use data as well as various data analytics products and services, we empower people worldwide to make fact-based decisions. Founded in Hamburg in 2007, we have quickly grown into a global company with offices in major cities such as London, New York, Berlin and Tokyo. And we still have a lot of plans. Our constant growth does not only prove our success, but also keeps creating new development and career opportunities for our employees. We value and celebrate our diverse culture. You are welcome here for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or whether you prefer bar graphs to pie charts. Your story matters – keep writing it as part of our team. Are you ready to join us? Your job As a Senior Data Analyst in the Data Analytics team, you are the driving force behind transforming complex data into clear, actionable insights and ensure that stakeholders across Statista can make confident, data-driven decisions. Plan, manage, and coordinate analytics and reporting projects, including timelines, stakeholders, and deliverables Serve as the central point of contact for senior stakeholders regarding KPIs, performance, quality, and customer behavior Understand stakeholder problems, hypotheses, and decision needs through discussions and workshops, and translate qualitative issues into clear analytical questions, metrics, and reporting requirements Analyze data in depth and derive concrete, actionable recommendations that support operational efficiency and growth objectives Advise senior stakeholders to enable data-driven decision-making and present results clearly, structured, and concisely for different audience groups Collaborate with cross-functional teams to identify opportunities for process improvement and deliver the foundation for scalable, data-driven solutions Your profile 4 years of professional experience in data analysis and/or consultancy Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple projects independently Experience in writing SQL queries and working with databases such as Amazon Redshift or Snowflake Proficiency in Microsoft Office, particularly advanced Excel skills Excellent verbal and written communication skills in English, with the ability to convey complex findings to both technical and non-technical stakeholders A strong analytical mindset paired with a structured, solution-oriented way of working Familiarity with programming languages like Python is a plus What we offer In addition to our great team, culture, and our shared goal of empowering people with data, there are many other things that make Statista a great place to work! Join us and benefit from: Work from abroad up to 30 calendar days a year Hybrid work and flex-time International team and social events Subsidized urban mobility and access to fitness and wellness options Free access to Langdock and all its amazing functionalities Career & training opportunities Attractive locations and modern offices Mental health support with OpenUp Some of the benefits listed here apply only to the German entity and to Junior-level roles or above. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
