    schema:description "<h2>Your Role</h2> <p>As our <strong>Senior Maintenance Manager (all genders)</strong>, you will be responsible for ensuring the reliable and efficient operation of our highly automated production facilities at our <strong>Barleben site near Magdeburg</strong>. Together with your Engineering team, you will ensure that our technical equipment remains safe, reliable, and available at all times.</p> <p>Working closely with Production, Supply Chain, and Engineering, you will develop future-oriented maintenance strategies, optimize technical processes, and create the conditions for smooth and efficient production. Through your leadership, technical expertise, and passion for Operational Excellence, you will make a significant contribution to the success of our production site.</p> <hr> <h2>What You'll Do</h2> <ul> <li> <p>Lead, develop, and inspire a team of Maintenance Supervisors, Automation Engineers, and Technicians while fostering a culture of collaboration, safety, and continuous improvement.</p> </li> <li> <p>Take ownership of the technical availability and reliability of our production equipment by continuously developing and optimizing our maintenance strategy to sustainably minimize downtime.</p> </li> <li> <p>Monitor and analyze key performance indicators (KPIs), including equipment availability, maintenance costs, and technical efficiency, and translate insights into impactful improvement initiatives.</p> </li> <li> <p>Plan and coordinate preventive and corrective maintenance activities to ensure reliable, efficient, and cost-effective plant operations.</p> </li> <li> <p>Collaborate closely with Production, Supply Chain, Engineering, and Procurement to develop technical solutions that continuously improve production performance.</p> </li> <li> <p>Lead the implementation and commissioning of new production equipment and automation solutions while ensuring compliance with all safety, quality, and regulatory requirements.</p> </li> <li> <p>Manage external service providers and suppliers, building long-term, trusted partnerships that support operational excellence.</p> </li> <li> <p>Drive the professional and personal development of your team while fostering a high-performance, motivating work environment.</p> </li> <li> <p>Ensure compliance with all legal requirements and internal standards related to occupational health and safety, food safety, quality, and compliance.</p> </li> <li> <p>Analyze technical failures, implement sustainable root-cause solutions, and lead cross-functional improvement and capital investment projects.</p> </li> <li> <p>Actively contribute to cross-site projects and strategic initiatives, helping shape the future development of our production network.</p> </li> </ul> <hr> <h2>What You'll Bring</h2> <ul> <li> <p>Bachelor's or Master's degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Automation Engineering, Mechatronics, or a comparable technical discipline.</p> </li> <li> <p>Several years of experience in maintenance or technical management within a manufacturing environment, ideally in the food, beverage, or FMCG industry.</p> </li> <li> <p>Proven leadership experience with a passion for developing, coaching, and motivating high-performing teams.</p> </li> <li> <p>Strong expertise in maintenance management as well as the maintenance and optimization of automated production systems.</p> </li> <li> <p>Experience with KPI management, project management, and the successful implementation of Operational Excellence and Continuous Improvement initiatives.</p> </li> <li> <p>Strong analytical, structured, and solution-oriented mindset combined with a hands-on approach.</p> </li> <li> <p>Excellent communication skills with the ability to explain technical topics clearly to a wide range of stakeholders.</p> </li> <li> <p>Proficiency in Microsoft Office; experience with Google Workspace and Dematic automation systems is considered an advantage.</p> </li> <li> <p>Solid knowledge of relevant occupational health and safety, food safety, quality, and compliance standards and regulations.</p> </li> <li> <p>Excellent organizational skills and the ability to prioritize effectively in a dynamic production environment.</p> </li> <li> <p>Passion for Operational Excellence, technical innovation, and the continuous development of people and processes.</p> </li> <li> <p>Fluency in German and good written and spoken English skills.</p> </li> </ul> <hr> <h2>What We Offer</h2> <ul> <li> <p>A modern workplace at an innovative and growing production site in <strong>Barleben near Magdeburg</strong>.</p> </li> <li> <p>A motivated team with short decision-making paths and plenty of room to make an impact.</p> </li> <li> <p>Attractive discounts on HelloFresh meal kits.</p> </li> <li> <p>Comprehensive learning and development opportunities through internal training and personalized development programs.</p> </li> <li> <p>A structured onboarding program to ensure a successful start.</p> </li> <li> <p>A competitive compensation package.</p> </li> <li> <p>30 days of annual leave.</p> </li> <li> <p>Subsidized Germany Ticket (Deutschlandticket).</p> </li> <li> <p>Company pension scheme.</p> </li> <li> <p>Discounted fitness memberships.</p> </li> <li> <p>High-quality personal protective equipment.</p> </li> <li> <p>Regular team events and many additional employee benefits.</p> </li> </ul> <hr> <h2>Hungry for More?</h2> <p>Then we'd love to hear from you! Please submit your application <strong>without a photo and without providing information about your nationality, gender, or other personal characteristics.</strong> You are, of course, welcome to voluntarily include language certificates as well as proof of your residence and work permit.</p> <p>We look forward to getting to know you!</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>#JD1001</strong><br><strong>#barnmaintenance</strong></p> Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-hellofresh ;
