    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "senior-ui-engineer-6-month-ftc-remote-or-onsite-london-uk-458163" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-23"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "The Space Rangers team are recruiting a 6 Month Fixed Term Contract (FTC) Senior UI Engineer to join a London based Game Studio! Location: UK Remote OR London, Bromley (on-site) The Role Space Rangers is partnering with a AAA game development studio to recruit a Senior UI Engineer. This role is essential to bring the UI user experience vision for their projects to life! Senior UI Engineers can scrutinise a UI design and identify the technical components needed to build a user interface. Working closely with the UI team and other development disciplines, they design and implement robust and performant UI frameworks and specialised UI widgets. They are proactive at planning and estimating their own and their team’s work which aligns with product specifications and project milestones. Our client’s Senior UI Engineers are afforded a high degree of autonomy and are trusted to know best how to complete their tasks. They effectively communicate elegant solutions to complex problems and work with the project team to ensure the delivery of a quality player experience. They enjoy working as part of a team in a friendly and collaborative atmosphere where they have the freedom to grow their technical knowledge and savour a technical challenge. They always look for ways to push themselves and their projects further and are encouraged to pass their experience on to other members of the team. Our client believes that levelling up skills is an essential part of the job, offering regular training opportunities and mentorship to all their Senior UI Engineers. You Have: A strong background in UI engineering for games; you have worked on at least one commercial project from concept through to shipping Advanced knowledge of C++, with relevant professional experience Practical UI implementation knowledge; you have worked within UI engineering teams to develop interfaces that follow best practices and technical intent A can-do attitude and strong interpersonal skills; you love collaborating with development disciplines to design and implement systems Strong time management and organisational skills; you can support others in getting the job done without supervision Effective communication and presentation skills; you can present ideas clearly to audiences of all experience levels A real enthusiasm for game UI Bonus Points for: Experience with Unreal Engine and Unreal Motion Graphics (UMG) Experience with accommodating a variety of player accessibility needs WHAT WE CAN OFFER: Competitive Salary and Benefits Package: Your health and wellbeing is important to us, so we offer a variety of benefits including: Enhanced Private Pension Scheme Private Medical Insurance Group Life Assurance Competitive holiday + studio wide closures in summer and winter Gym Membership Allowance Free Eye Tests Free on-site parking Electric Car Scheme Season Ticket Loans A FRIENDLY NOTE FROM THE RECRUITMENT TEAM: Let us do the work for you: Even if your profile isn’t an exact match for all of the qualifications listed above, we still want you to apply. Our team members come from a variety of different industries, not all of which are immediately relevant to game or software development, and we welcome all candidates of similarly varied backgrounds, communities, and identities. Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-rocketsciencegg ;
