    schema:datePosted "2026-08-23"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "<p>Optiver is looking for a Senior Digital Assets Software Engineer to join our Digital Assets Tech Team in London. In this role, you’ll build and evolve trading systems for cryptocurrency markets, working closely with traders and researchers to deliver solutions in a fast-moving and constantly changing environment.</p> <p>You’ll play a key role in building out our digital assets platform, helping shape both the technology and engineering practices from the ground up. You’ll work side-by-side with traders and researchers, iterating quickly on ideas and translating market insights into production systems. From integrating with major centralised exchanges to improving system reliability in real-world conditions, your work will directly impact how we trade in this rapidly growing space.</p> <p><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p> <ul> <li>Design and build trading systems for digital asset markets</li> <li>Develop and manage connectivity to centralised exchanges such as Binance, Deribit, and OKX</li> <li>Work directly with traders and researchers to prototype and iterate on trading strategies</li> <li>Improve system reliability through automation, monitoring, and robust recovery mechanisms</li> <li>Troubleshoot issues across trading systems and exchange integrations</li> <li>Contribute to architecture and help shape the digital assets platform</li> <li>Take ownership of production systems and drive continuous improvements</li> </ul> <p><strong>Who you are</strong></p> <ul> <li>5+ years of experience in software engineering, ideally in trading, crypto, or other real-time systems</li> <li>Strong C++ development skills, with experience building reliable production systems</li> <li>Hands-on experience integrating with centralised cryptocurrency exchanges (e.g., Binance, Deribit, OKX)</li> <li>Experience working with cloud technologies (e.g., AWS, GCP, or similar) is a plus</li> <li>Good understanding of distributed systems, networking, and failure handling</li> <li>Strong problem-solving skills and ability to operate effectively in fast-paced environments</li> <li>Comfortable working in a highly collaborative environment, partnering directly with traders and researchers</li> <li>Able to translate ambiguous trading requirements into practical engineering solutions</li> <li>Ownership-driven mindset with a focus on building resilient systems</li> </ul> <p><strong>Who we are&nbsp;</strong></p> <p>At Optiver, our mission is to continuously improve the market. By providing liquidity and accurate pricing in various financial instruments, to multiple exchanges across the world, we participate in the safeguarding of healthy and efficient markets.</p> <p><strong>What you’ll get</strong></p> <p>You’ll join a culture of collaboration and excellence, where you’ll be surrounded by curious thinkers and creative problem solvers. Motivated by a passion for continuous improvement, you’ll thrive in a supportive, high-performing environment alongside talented colleagues, working collectively to tackle the toughest problems in the financial markets.</p> <p>In addition, you’ll receive:</p> <ul> <li>A performance-based bonus structure, enabling all of our employees to benefit from our global profit pool.</li> <li>27 paid vacation days plus all UK public holidays.</li> <li>Daily breakfast and lunch, along with support on commuting expenses.</li> <li>Private medical insurance, pension scheme, and ClassPass fitness membership.</li> <li>Training and continuous learning opportunities, including access to conferences and tech events.</li> <li>International transfer opportunities for global career growth.</li> </ul> <p><strong>How to apply</strong></p> <p>Apply directly via the form below. If you have any questions feel free to contact our Recruitment team via ----- <p>Please note:</p> <ul> <li>We do not require any assistance from third-parties including agencies in the recruitment of this role</li> <li>We cannot accept applications via email</li> </ul> <p><strong>Diversity statement</strong></p> <p>Optiver is committed to <a href=\"https://optiver.com/diversity-statement/?_gl=1*bh82o8*_up*MQ..&amp;gclid=EAIaIQobChMItNH9v-THiQMVyJZQBh1Kbw3YEAAYASABEgI0z_D_BwE\">diversity and inclusion</a>.</p> Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
